Acceptance criteria verified by this task: AC-27, AC-28, AC-30, AC-36, AC-37,
AC-38, AC-39, AC-41, AC-42.

PII posture: omission, not masking. The portal names no taxpayer type and holds
no SIN, so there is nothing to mask; a second masking helper is what every
module's instructions forbid. AC-37 checks the live response bodies, not just
the source.

Non-vacuity. Every assertion in this suite is negative — it passes when a
pattern finds nothing — so a typo'd or over-escaped regex would pass silently
and forever while approving exactly what it was written to catch. Three
protections:
  - EveryForbiddenPattern_ActuallyMatchesAViolatingLine pairs sixteen patterns
    with a line each MUST match;
  - the nine-digit pattern is checked in both directions: it must match a
    SIN-shaped literal and must NOT match the shell's "initial-scale=1";
  - the scanner guard proves the walk sees exactly Program.cs,
    ModuleRegistration.cs, and PortalContent.cs, and that the comment filter is
    really stripping comments rather than "executable lines only" silently
    scanning whole files.
As in T04, production code was NOT temporarily broken to prove these: T05 owns
no production file and mutating one would violate declared-file ownership.

AddServerHeader = false is asserted twice — once on the wire (no Server header
on the response) and once in source, because TestServer does not use Kestrel and
structurally cannot verify the real deployment behaviour.

ENVIRONMENT: the Smart App Control block that stopped T02 and T04 did not recur.
The human turned Smart App Control off during T04 (state now 0), and every suite
in this task ran on first execution.

  The hazard first flagged in T02 remains unfixed and is not this task's to fix:
  `dotnet test TaxAI.sln` returns exit code 0 when an assembly is skipped, so a
  green exit code alone is not proof that every test ran.

Merged by: not merged — awaiting human review. Agents never merge.
